{"id":"other-pay-against-counties","tier":"REDFLAG","title":"Pay outside salary and overtime: San Francisco against the largest counties","question":"Is San Francisco’s “other pay” (premiums, incentives, one-time payments) and lump-sum pay large against California’s big county payrolls?","finding":"In 2024 San Francisco’s other pay plus lump sums came to 5.4% of regular pay (5,871 dollars per paid position), 10 of 13 against the 12 county payrolls compared; highest: Ventura 13.0%, Sacramento 12.2%, Contra Costa 8.9%.","how":"State Controller raw export, 2024. Other pay and lump-sum pay are the export’s own columns, each divided by regular pay. Counties are the ten largest by paid positions plus the Bay Area counties. The export does not say whether a year is a calendar or a fiscal year. San Francisco’s overtime here is $480.3 million for 2024; the City’s own payroll file has $468.9 million for fiscal 2024 and $471.0 million for fiscal 2025, so the two sources are close but not the same and are not mixed in any one figure.","limits":"Employers do not split pay between “other” and “lump sum” the same way: a leave payout may be in either. Neither column says what the payment was for. A position is a row, not a person.","columns":[{"k":"employer","t":"Employer","type":"org"},{"k":"year","t":"Year","type":"year"},{"k":"positions","t":"Paid positions","type":"int"},{"k":"otherShare","t":"Other pay as share of regular pay","type":"pct"},{"k":"lumpShare","t":"Lump sums as share of regular pay","type":"pct"},{"k":"otherPer","t":"Other pay and lump sums per paid position","type":"usd"},{"k":"otShare","t":"Overtime as share of regular pay","type":"pct"}],"rows":[{"employer":"Ventura","year":2024,"positions":12162,"regular":863371796,"overtime":98460854,"other":78462340,"lumpSum":33598861,"otPer":8096,"otherPer":9214,"otShare":0.114,"otherShare":0.0909,"lumpShare":0.0389,"outliers":117,"outPer1000":13.07,"full":8953},{"employer":"Sacramento","year":2024,"positions":15267,"regul